>
> Not a bad choice, but if I were you, I would consider:

> 2) an amulet of unchanging. - allows you to stay in crystal golem form
> permanently.

One of the best wish for doppelgangers.

> 3) A wand of polymorph - polypiling is not as useful anymore, but it
> still can be great for collecting spells and immediate use
> potions/scrolls.

IMHO easier to find before it really becomes useful than the amulet.

> The useful spells you should know include:
> 1) Charm Monster
> 2) Haste self
> 3) Identify
> 4) magic mapping

I almost neverused spell of ID since I usually manage to id almost  
everything before being able to reliably cast it.

> Lets talk medium-term strategy now.  At this stage, you should be
> getting ready to do the quest.  The best place to stock up for this is
> at the Black Market.  As a doppelganger, you have an ideal way of
> robbing the BM of everything you can carry.  So here is the plan:
>
> Find the portal to the Black Market.
> Create an Elbereth-protected cache next to the portal
> Put your heavy stuff into the cache.

Actually, put everything there but a few pieces of armor/weapon (to kill  
random monsters), a blessed BoH and maybe some rings (slow digestion, free  
action, polycontrol) and amulets (unchanging). All the rest is quite  
useless and can usually be found in the market if you really need it  
(food, even healing sources).

> Enter the BM and quaff a blessed potion of object detection.

What the use ?

> Collect and bless all of the Identify scrolls in the market.
> Use these scrolls to identify all unknown items in the market.

Again, not really useful, I usually collect everything midly interesting  
in the market (at this stage of the game, scrolls, potions, amulets,  
wands, spellbooks plus a few misc items usually) and go through sorting  
process later (and the not so useful items make great polyfodder...) Btw,  
you can price-id in the black market, price are just 50 time (or something  
like that) more expensive.

> Collect ALL useful items (all potions, scrolls, wands, spellbooks,
> artifacts, magical armor, tools, rings, amulets, etc.)
> Sell your identified gems to get all of Sam's gold, then get your gems
> again.
> Be VERY careful not to have a BoHolding explosion or trapped chest
> accident.

Indeed. I once had a bill of more than a million zormkids for nothing...

> Polymorph into a xorn, and exit the market from the upper corner
> directly into the portal.

No. Step on the square just south of the portal and then go through the  
portal. Thus, monsters will be generated inside the market and won't  
follow you outside.
Depending on where on the dungeon level the portal is, you may also want  
to destroy/hide it to avoid later trouble (like accidentally walking on it  
during a summoning storm after double trouble...)

> For the quest, you have a few options.  Have you learned how to use the
> "chained blitz" technique yet?

Free action is a strongly recommended option. Gauntlets of defense is also  
more than nice. Free action + potion of paralysis is always a recommended  
option. potion of invulnerability is also an option.

Concerning chained blitz, I must confess that even after playing quite a  
lot of monk (1 ascended, 1 killed by Demogorgon, 2 or 3 reached the  
quests), I never really manage to used it properly...

